---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Field from '../components/Field.astro';
import ReachMap from '../components/ReachMap.astro';
import Action from '../components/Action.astro';
import { COMPANY, PHONE_HREF } from '../data/company.ts';
import { PAGES } from '../data/site.ts';

const meta = PAGES[1]!;
---
<Base title={meta.title} description={meta.description}>
  <Field tone="forest" reveal={false}>
    <div class="hero">
      <h1>A redwood mill in Mendocino County.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Agwood Mill &amp; Lumber is a family-owned sawmill in {COMPANY.address.locality},
        supplying redwood wholesale to the Northern California trade.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Field>

  <Field tone="paper">
    <h2>One species, run properly.</h2>
    <p class="prose gap">
      Redwood is the only timber we mill. That is a choice about attention rather
      than a limit on capacity: grading redwood consistently means knowing how this
      wood moves, splits and seasons, and that knowledge does not transfer from one
      species to the next.
    </p>
    <p class="prose">
      We sell to lumber retailers and distributors across Northern California. They
      resell what we grade, under their own name, to customers we never meet. That
      only works if what is on the sticker is what is in the pack.
    </p>
  </Field>

  <!-- The map earns the dark field: it is the one graphic on the site and it wants
       the ground that makes it read. -->
  <Field tone="forest">
    <div class="reach">
      <div class="reach-txt">
        <h2>Where it goes.</h2>
        <p class="prose gap">
          Ukiah sits in Mendocino County, inside a hundred miles of most of the
          Northern California lumber trade.
        </p>
        <p class="prose">
          Close enough to the coast for the redwood, close enough to the valley for
          the yards that sell it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reach-map"><ReachMap /></div>
    </div>
  </Field>

  <Field tone="paper">
    <h2 class="ttl label">Regulation</h2>
    <!--
      Deliberately narrow, and it must stay that way. The client approved stating
      the Forest Practice Act as jurisdictional context. Its permitted scope is
      exactly that: a fact about California law. It may NOT be rewritten to describe
      Agwood's own sourcing or to imply a certification the company does not hold —
      we do not know where their logs come from. The second sentence is the safety
      valve and must not be deleted to tidy the paragraph.
    -->
    <p class="prose">
      Timber harvested on private and industrial land in California is governed by
      the California Forest Practice Act, which requires approved harvest plans
      covering water quality, erosion and replanting. Agwood holds no FSC or SFI
      certification and does not claim one.
    </p>
  </Field>

  <Field tone="deep">
    <h2>Talk to the mill.</h2>
    <p class="prose gap">The office answers the telephone Monday to Friday, seven to four.</p>
    <p class="cta"><Action href={PHONE_HREF}>Call the mill — {COMPANY.phone}</Action></p>
  </Field>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero h1 { max-width: 15ch; font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 6.2vw, 3.8rem); }
  .hero .lede { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 42ch; }
  .ttl { color: var(--russet); margin-bottom: 1.2rem; font-family: var(--font-body); }
  .gap { margin-bottom: var(--stack); }
  .cta { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .reach { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); align-items: center; }
  .reach-txt h2 { max-width: 14ch; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .reach { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .reach-map { max-width: 30rem; }
  }
</style>
